# Per-path token ceilings, gated by `itok check` (pinned tier, V5). Only
# registered paths are checked; everything else is unchecked (V10). This
# is itok checking itself -- the dogfood.
# A CEILING that forces a REVIEW, not one that forces a shrink (V84).
#
# History: 19,542 -> 20,500 (T49) -> 21,500 -> 25,000 -> 27,500. It has now
# bitten four times on spec ADDITIONS, and every time the addition was
# correct: the spec grows because the project does (101 invariants). A
# ceiling set a hair above current turns every legitimate addition into a
# raise, and a threshold raised reflexively is the noise-nobody-reads
# failure V71 warns about -- it trains the reflex instead of catching the
# problem.
#
# So: real headroom (~13%), and the actual control is T70's scripted
# compaction, which is now overdue rather than pending. The ceiling
# catches RUNAWAY growth; T70 pays the debt. Two different jobs, and
# conflating them made the ceiling useless at both.
#
# 25,000 -> 27,500 was NOT a reflexive raise, and the distinction is the
# one the paragraph above draws. The ceiling had decayed to 0.3% headroom
# (24,927 of 25,000) -- precisely the "hair above current" state it warns
# against -- and what it was blocking was not growth but RECORDING: five
# measured defects and four designs could not be written into §B/§T. An
# unrecordable defect is strictly worse than a larger spec, because §B is
# the memory that stops recurrence (V69's false-assurance argument, from
# the other side). Restores ~10% headroom. T70 is still the control, and
# this buys it time rather than replacing it.
#
# NOT a fit constraint. SPEC.md is 2.5% of a 1M window and fits every
# model we target. The ceiling exists for the re-billing INTEGRAL (V84,
# V94): held from turn 1 it bills ~9M itok per session, on free inference
# and paid alike. Size is not the cost; size x turns is.
SPEC.md    27500
README.md  4k
